IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `act-nouns`
IMPORT `act-interpretation-time`

-- Legislation Act 2001 (Australian Capital Territory), chapter 13: Structure of Acts and statutory instruments (Parts 13.1 and 13.2).
--
-- Part 13.1 says which material is part of an Act or instrument (ss 126, 127).
-- Part 13.2 says what a definition, a signpost definition and an example are (ss 130 to 132), what a penalty unit is (s 133),
-- and how a penalty stated in a law is read (ss 134, 135).
-- s 126 (2), the rule for a heading to a section or subsection, is computed from dates in `act-interpretation-time.l4`;
-- its answer is an input to `s 126, s 127: the material is part of the Act or instrument`.
-- The sections that say they are determinative provisions (ss 126 (9), 127 (7), 132 (4), 133 (4), 134 (7), 135 (6)) are in `act-determinative.l4`.
--
-- A rule that says a thing "is part of", "is not part of" or "is not affected" answers JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE for the kinds of thing it names,
-- and NOTHING for a kind it does not name.
-- A "may" or "includes" rule answers JUST TRUE when its conditions are met, and NOTHING otherwise.
-- A "means" definition answers TRUE or FALSE.

§ `Legislation Act 2001 (ACT): chapter 13, Structure of Acts and statutory instruments`

§§ `Part 13.1: General`

-- src:1611 | In this chapter:
-- src:1612 | law means an Act, subordinate law or disallowable instrument.
-- src:1613 | Note A reference to an Act, subordinate law or disallowable instrument includes a reference to a provision of the Act, law or instrument (see s 7, s 8 and s 9).
@ref s 125 (src:1611-1613)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of Act or instrument`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 125: the kind of document is a law for chapter 13` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `an Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a subordinate law` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a disallowable instrument` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a notifiable instrument` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a commencement notice` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a statutory instrument of another kind` THEN FALSE

-- The kinds of material that ss 126 and 127 name.
-- `material of some other kind` stands for anything they do not name (the sections of the Act or instrument are not named, for example).
-- src:1616 | (1) A heading to a chapter, part, division, subdivision, schedule, or another provision (other than a section or subsection), of or to an Act or statutory instrument is part of the Act or instrument.
@ref s 126 (1) (src:1616-1616)
-- src:1617 | (2) A heading to a section or subsection of an Act or statutory instrument is part of the Act or instrument if—
-- src:1618 | (a) the Act was enacted, or the instrument was made, after 1 January 2000; or
-- src:1619 | (b) the heading was amended or inserted into the Act or instrument after 1 January 2000.
@ref s 126 (2) (src:1617-1619)
-- src:1620 | (3) A preamble or other recital to an Act or statutory instrument is part of the Act or instrument.
-- src:1621 | (4) An example or diagram in an Act or statutory instrument is part of the Act or instrument.
-- src:1622 | (5) A schedule, dictionary or appendix to an Act or statutory instrument is part of the Act or instrument.
-- src:1623 | (6) Punctuation in an Act or statutory instrument is part of the Act or instrument.
-- src:1624 | (7) A provision number in an Act or statutory instrument is part of the Act or instrument.
@ref s 126 (3) to (7) (src:1620-1624)
-- src:1631 | (1) A footnote, endnote, or other note, in or to an Act or statutory instrument is not part of the Act or instrument.
-- src:1632 | (2) A table of contents (however described), or reader’s guide or index, in or to an Act or statutory instrument is not part of the Act or instrument.
-- src:1633 | (3) A heading to a section or subsection of an Act or statutory instrument is not part of the Act or instrument if section 126 (2) does not apply to the heading.
@ref s 127 (1) to (3) (src:1631-1633)
DECLARE `Kind of material in or to an Act or instrument` IS ONE OF
    `a heading to a chapter, part, division, subdivision, schedule, or another provision (other than a section or subsection)`
    `a heading to a section or subsection`
    `a preamble or other recital`
    `an example or diagram`
    `a schedule, dictionary or appendix`
    `punctuation`
    `a provision number`
    `a footnote, endnote or other note`
    `a table of contents, reader's guide or index`
    `material of some other kind`

-- s 127 (3): a heading to a section or subsection is not part of the Act or instrument if s 126 (2) does not apply to it.
-- So the same input, the answer of the s 126 (2) rule, decides both ways.
-- src:1616 | (1) A heading to a chapter, part, division, subdivision, schedule, or another provision (other than a section or subsection), of or to an Act or statutory instrument is part of the Act or instrument.
@ref s 126 (1) (src:1616-1616)
-- src:1617 | (2) A heading to a section or subsection of an Act or statutory instrument is part of the Act or instrument if—
-- src:1618 | (a) the Act was enacted, or the instrument was made, after 1 January 2000; or
-- src:1619 | (b) the heading was amended or inserted into the Act or instrument after 1 January 2000.
@ref s 126 (2) (src:1617-1619)
-- src:1620 | (3) A preamble or other recital to an Act or statutory instrument is part of the Act or instrument.
-- src:1621 | (4) An example or diagram in an Act or statutory instrument is part of the Act or instrument.
-- src:1622 | (5) A schedule, dictionary or appendix to an Act or statutory instrument is part of the Act or instrument.
-- src:1623 | (6) Punctuation in an Act or statutory instrument is part of the Act or instrument.
-- src:1624 | (7) A provision number in an Act or statutory instrument is part of the Act or instrument.
@ref s 126 (3) to (7) (src:1620-1624)
-- src:1631 | (1) A footnote, endnote, or other note, in or to an Act or statutory instrument is not part of the Act or instrument.
-- src:1632 | (2) A table of contents (however described), or reader’s guide or index, in or to an Act or statutory instrument is not part of the Act or instrument.
-- src:1633 | (3) A heading to a section or subsection of an Act or statutory instrument is not part of the Act or instrument if section 126 (2) does not apply to the heading.
@ref s 127 (1) to (3) (src:1631-1633)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of material in or to an Act or instrument`, theHeadingIsPartOfTheActOrInstrumentUnderSection126Subsection2 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 126, s 127: the material is part of the Act or instrument` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a heading to a chapter, part, division, subdivision, schedule, or another provision (other than a section or subsection)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a heading to a section or subsection` THEN JUST theHeadingIsPartOfTheActOrInstrumentUnderSection126Subsection2
    WHEN `a preamble or other recital` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an example or diagram` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a schedule, dictionary or appendix` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `punctuation` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a provision number` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a footnote, endnote or other note` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `a table of contents, reader's guide or index` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `material of some other kind` THEN NOTHING

-- src:1625 | (8) In applying this section to an Act or statutory instrument that is divided otherwise than into sections, a reference to a section or subsection is a reference to a corresponding provision of the Act or instrument.
-- src:1626 | Note A reference to an Act or statutory instrument includes a reference to a provision of the Act or instrument (see s 7 and s 13).
@ref s 126 (8) (src:1625-1626)
-- src:1636 | (6) In applying this section to an Act or statutory instrument that is divided otherwise than into sections, a reference to a section or subsection is a reference to a corresponding provision of the Act or instrument.
-- src:1637 | Note A reference to an Act or statutory instrument includes a reference to a provision of the Act or instrument (see s 7 and s 13).
@ref s 127 (6) (src:1636-1637)
GIVEN theActOrInstrumentIsDividedOtherwiseThanIntoSections IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 126 (8), s 127 (6): a reference to a section or subsection is a reference to a corresponding provision` MEANS
    IF   theActOrInstrumentIsDividedOtherwiseThanIntoSections
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1634 | (4) This section does not prevent the amendment of a note, table, guide, index or heading mentioned in subsection (1), (2) or (3).
@ref s 127 (4) (src:1634-1634)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 127 (4): this section prevents the amendment of a note, table, guide, index or heading` MEANS FALSE

-- src:1635 | (5) However, such a note, table, guide or index does not become part of the Act or statutory instrument because it is amended or inserted by an Act or instrument.
@ref s 127 (5) (src:1635-1635)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of material in or to an Act or instrument`, theMaterialIsAmendedOrInsertedByAnActOrInstrument IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 127 (5): the note, table, guide or index becomes part of the Act or instrument because it is amended or inserted` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a footnote, endnote or other note` THEN
        IF   theMaterialIsAmendedOrInsertedByAnActOrInstrument
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHEN `a table of contents, reader's guide or index` THEN
        IF   theMaterialIsAmendedOrInsertedByAnActOrInstrument
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE NOTHING
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `Part 13.2: Particular kinds of provisions`

-- src:1644 | A definition is a provision (however expressed) of an Act or statutory instrument that—
-- src:1645 | (a) gives a meaning to a term; or
-- src:1646 | (b) limits or extends the meaning of a term.
@ref s 130 (src:1644-1646)
GIVEN theProvisionIsOfAnActOrStatutoryInstrument IS A BOOLEAN, theProvisionGivesAMeaningToATerm IS A BOOLEAN, theProvisionLimitsOrExtendsTheMeaningOfATerm IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 130: the provision is a definition` MEANS
    theProvisionIsOfAnActOrStatutoryInstrument AND (theProvisionGivesAMeaningToATerm OR theProvisionLimitsOrExtendsTheMeaningOfATerm)

-- What the signpost definition gives the term.
-- "As in force from time to time" is part of every answer; it is not a separate input because the text allows no other.
-- src:1664 | (1) In an Act or statutory instrument, a definition of a term that includes the word ‘see’ followed by a reference to a law or instrument (a signpost definition) means the term has the same meaning as the term (or, if the reference includes a reference to the definition of another term, that term) has in the law or instrument, as in force from time to time.
-- src:1665 | Examples
-- src:1666 | 1 A signpost definition ‘food—see section 10.’ in the dictionary to an Act means that the word ‘food’ when used in the Act has the same meaning as it has in section 10, as in force from time to time.
-- src:1667 | 2 A signpost definition ‘injury—see the XYZ Act 2001, dictionary.’ in the dictionary to another Act means that the word ‘injury’, when used in the other Act, has the same meaning as it has in the definition of injury in the XYZ Act 2001, dictionary, as in force from time to time.
-- src:1668 | 3 A signpost definition ‘Work Safety Council—see the XYZ Act 2000, dictionary, definition of council.’ means that the expression ‘Work Safety Council’ has the same meaning as the word ‘council’ has in the definition of council in the XYZ Act 2000, dictionary, as in force from time to time.
@ref s 131 (1) (src:1664-1668)
DECLARE `Meaning a signpost definition gives a term` IS ONE OF
    `the meaning the term itself has in the law or instrument referred to`
    `the meaning the other term named in the reference has in the law or instrument referred to`

-- src:1664 | (1) In an Act or statutory instrument, a definition of a term that includes the word ‘see’ followed by a reference to a law or instrument (a signpost definition) means the term has the same meaning as the term (or, if the reference includes a reference to the definition of another term, that term) has in the law or instrument, as in force from time to time.
-- src:1665 | Examples
-- src:1666 | 1 A signpost definition ‘food—see section 10.’ in the dictionary to an Act means that the word ‘food’ when used in the Act has the same meaning as it has in section 10, as in force from time to time.
-- src:1667 | 2 A signpost definition ‘injury—see the XYZ Act 2001, dictionary.’ in the dictionary to another Act means that the word ‘injury’, when used in the other Act, has the same meaning as it has in the definition of injury in the XYZ Act 2001, dictionary, as in force from time to time.
-- src:1668 | 3 A signpost definition ‘Work Safety Council—see the XYZ Act 2000, dictionary, definition of council.’ means that the expression ‘Work Safety Council’ has the same meaning as the word ‘council’ has in the definition of council in the XYZ Act 2000, dictionary, as in force from time to time.
@ref s 131 (1) (src:1664-1668)
GIVEN theDefinitionIncludesTheWordSeeFollowedByAReferenceToALawOrInstrument IS A BOOLEAN, theReferenceIncludesAReferenceToTheDefinitionOfAnotherTerm IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Meaning a signpost definition gives a term`
`s 131 (1): the meaning a signpost definition gives the term` MEANS
    IF   NOT theDefinitionIncludesTheWordSeeFollowedByAReferenceToALawOrInstrument
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF   theReferenceIncludesAReferenceToTheDefinitionOfAnotherTerm
         THEN JUST `the meaning the other term named in the reference has in the law or instrument referred to`
         ELSE JUST `the meaning the term itself has in the law or instrument referred to`

-- Section 47 is outside this encoding's scope; the sections a rule is subject to are listed, as s 73 (5) does in the commencement module.
-- src:1669 | (2) This section is subject to section 47 (Statutory instrument may make provision by applying law or instrument).
@ref s 131 (2) (src:1669-1669)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 131 (2): the sections that s 131 is subject to` MEANS LIST "47"

-- src:1676 | (1) An example in an Act or statutory instrument—
-- src:1677 | (a) is not exhaustive; and
@ref s 132 (1) (a) (src:1676-1677)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 132 (1) (a): an example is exhaustive` MEANS FALSE

-- src:1676 | (1) An example in an Act or statutory instrument—
@ref s 132 (1) (b) (src:1676-1676)
-- src:1678 | (b) may extend, but does not limit, the meaning of the Act or instrument, or the particular provision to which it relates.
@ref s 132 (1) (b) (src:1678-1678)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 132 (1) (b): an example may extend the meaning of the Act or instrument, or of the provision to which it relates` MEANS TRUE

-- src:1676 | (1) An example in an Act or statutory instrument—
@ref s 132 (1) (b) (src:1676-1676)
-- src:1678 | (b) may extend, but does not limit, the meaning of the Act or instrument, or the particular provision to which it relates.
@ref s 132 (1) (b) (src:1678-1678)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 132 (1) (b): an example limits the meaning of the Act or instrument, or of the provision to which it relates` MEANS FALSE

-- src:1679 | (2) An example may take either of the following forms:
-- src:1680 | (a) a statement at the end of the provision it illustrates (or at the end of a provision containing the provision it illustrates);
-- src:1681 | (b) a statement forming part of the text of a provision that illustrates the operation of the provision, whether or not the words ‘for example’ are used.
@ref s 132 (2) (src:1679-1681)
GIVEN theStatementIsAtTheEndOfTheProvisionItIllustratesOrOfAProvisionContainingIt IS A BOOLEAN, theStatementFormsPartOfTheTextOfAProvisionAndIllustratesItsOperation IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 132 (2): the statement has a form an example may take` MEANS
    IF   theStatementIsAtTheEndOfTheProvisionItIllustratesOrOfAProvisionContainingIt OR theStatementFormsPartOfTheTextOfAProvisionAndIllustratesItsOperation
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1682 | (3) Subsection (2) does not limit the form that an example may take.
@ref s 132 (3) (src:1682-1682)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 132 (3): subsection (2) limits the form that an example may take` MEANS FALSE

§§ `Section 133: Penalty units`

-- src:1687 | (1) In a law, if a penalty for an offence is expressed as a number (whether whole or fractional) of penalty units, the penalty for the offence is a fine of that number of penalty units.
@ref s 133 (1) (src:1687-1687)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of Act or instrument`, thePenaltyForTheOffenceIsExpressedAsANumberOfPenaltyUnits IS A BOOLEAN, numberOfPenaltyUnits IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 133 (1): the fine, in penalty units` MEANS
    IF   `s 125: the kind of document is a law for chapter 13` kind AND thePenaltyForTheOffenceIsExpressedAsANumberOfPenaltyUnits
    THEN JUST numberOfPenaltyUnits
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Kind of offender` IS ONE OF
    `an individual`
    `a corporation`
    `an offender who is neither an individual nor a corporation`

-- src:1688 | (2) A penalty unit is—
-- src:1689 | (a) for an offence committed by an individual—$160; or
-- src:1690 | (b) for an offence committed by a corporation—$810.
@ref s 133 (2) (src:1688-1690)
GIVEN offender IS A `Kind of offender`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 133 (2): the amount of a penalty unit, in dollars` MEANS
    CONSIDER offender
    WHEN `an individual` THEN JUST 160
    WHEN `a corporation` THEN JUST 810
    WHEN `an offender who is neither an individual nor a corporation` THEN NOTHING

-- src:1687 | (1) In a law, if a penalty for an offence is expressed as a number (whether whole or fractional) of penalty units, the penalty for the offence is a fine of that number of penalty units.
@ref s 133 (1) (src:1687-1687)
-- src:1688 | (2) A penalty unit is—
-- src:1689 | (a) for an offence committed by an individual—$160; or
-- src:1690 | (b) for an offence committed by a corporation—$810.
@ref s 133 (2) (src:1688-1690)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of Act or instrument`, offender IS A `Kind of offender`, thePenaltyForTheOffenceIsExpressedAsANumberOfPenaltyUnits IS A BOOLEAN, numberOfPenaltyUnits IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 133 (1), (2): the fine, in dollars` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 133 (1): the fine, in penalty units` kind thePenaltyForTheOffenceIsExpressedAsANumberOfPenaltyUnits numberOfPenaltyUnits
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST units THEN
        CONSIDER `s 133 (2): the amount of a penalty unit, in dollars` offender
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST amount THEN JUST (units TIMES amount)

-- "At least once every 4 years after the day this subsection commences" is read as successive periods of 4 years counted from that day.
-- The first review is due by the last day of the first period; the next by the last day of the second, and so on.
-- The other reading, 4 years after each review, is had by passing the day of the last review as the start and 1 as the period.
-- The last day comes from the time module (s 151), so it is NOTHING where that module is silent, as it is for years not starting on 1 January.
-- src:1691 | (3) The Attorney-General must review the amount of a penalty unit at least once every 4 years after the day this subsection commences.
@ref s 133 (3) (src:1691-1691)
GIVEN `the day the count of periods starts from` IS A DATE, `which period of 4 years, counting the first as 1` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 133 (3): the last day by which the Attorney-General must have reviewed the amount of a penalty unit` MEANS
    `s 151: the last day of a period of days, months or years that begins on or from a stated day` (4 TIMES `which period of 4 years, counting the first as 1`) years `beginning from or after a stated day` `the day the count of periods starts from`

§§ `Sections 134 and 135: penalties stated in a law`

-- src:1696 | (1) This section applies if a penalty (however expressed) is stated in a law—
-- src:1697 | (a) at the end of a section (whether or not the section is divided into subsections) and not expressed in a way that indicates that it applies only to a provision of the section; or
-- src:1698 | (b) at the end of a subsection (but not at the end of a section) and not expressed in a way that indicates that it applies only to a provision of the subsection; or
-- src:1699 | (c) at the end of a section or subsection and expressed in a way that indicates that it applies only to a provision of the section or subsection (the relevant provision).
@ref s 134 (1) (src:1696-1699)
-- src:1751 | (1) This section applies if a penalty (however expressed) is stated in a provision of a law other than at the end of a section or subsection.
@ref s 135 (1) (src:1751-1751)
DECLARE `Where a penalty is stated` IS ONE OF
    `at the end of a section`
    `at the end of a subsection but not at the end of a section`
    `in a provision, other than at the end of a section or subsection`

DECLARE `Section that governs a stated penalty` IS ONE OF
    `section 134 governs the penalty`
    `section 135 governs the penalty`

-- src:1696 | (1) This section applies if a penalty (however expressed) is stated in a law—
-- src:1697 | (a) at the end of a section (whether or not the section is divided into subsections) and not expressed in a way that indicates that it applies only to a provision of the section; or
-- src:1698 | (b) at the end of a subsection (but not at the end of a section) and not expressed in a way that indicates that it applies only to a provision of the subsection; or
-- src:1699 | (c) at the end of a section or subsection and expressed in a way that indicates that it applies only to a provision of the section or subsection (the relevant provision).
@ref s 134 (1) (src:1696-1699)
-- src:1751 | (1) This section applies if a penalty (however expressed) is stated in a provision of a law other than at the end of a section or subsection.
@ref s 135 (1) (src:1751-1751)
GIVEN where IS A `Where a penalty is stated`
GIVETH A `Section that governs a stated penalty`
`s 134 (1), s 135 (1): the section that governs the stated penalty` MEANS
    CONSIDER where
    WHEN `at the end of a section` THEN `section 134 governs the penalty`
    WHEN `at the end of a subsection but not at the end of a section` THEN `section 134 governs the penalty`
    WHEN `in a provision, other than at the end of a section or subsection` THEN `section 135 governs the penalty`

-- What the stated penalty is about, as s 134 (1) to (3) and s 135 (2), (3) read it.
DECLARE `What a stated penalty applies to` IS ONE OF
    `the whole section`
    `the whole subsection`
    `only the relevant provision of the section or subsection`
    `the provision in which the penalty is stated, or a stated part of it`

-- src:1696 | (1) This section applies if a penalty (however expressed) is stated in a law—
-- src:1697 | (a) at the end of a section (whether or not the section is divided into subsections) and not expressed in a way that indicates that it applies only to a provision of the section; or
-- src:1698 | (b) at the end of a subsection (but not at the end of a section) and not expressed in a way that indicates that it applies only to a provision of the subsection; or
-- src:1699 | (c) at the end of a section or subsection and expressed in a way that indicates that it applies only to a provision of the section or subsection (the relevant provision).
@ref s 134 (1) (src:1696-1699)
-- src:1713 | (2) If an offence is not expressly mentioned in the section, subsection or relevant provision, the penalty indicates that contravention of the section, subsection or relevant provision is an offence punishable on conviction as provided by subsection (4).
@ref s 134 (2) (src:1713-1713)
-- src:1722 | (3) If an offence is expressly mentioned in the section, subsection or relevant provision, the penalty indicates that the offence is punishable on conviction as provided by subsection (4).
@ref s 134 (3) (src:1722-1722)
-- src:1755 | (3) If an offence is not expressly mentioned in the provision, the penalty indicates that contravention of the provision (or a stated part of the provision) is an offence punishable on conviction as provided by subsection (4).
@ref s 135 (3) (src:1755-1755)
GIVEN where IS A `Where a penalty is stated`, theExpressionIndicatesThePenaltyAppliesOnlyToAProvisionOfTheSectionOrSubsection IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What a stated penalty applies to`
`s 134 (1) to (3), s 135 (3): what the stated penalty applies to` MEANS
    CONSIDER where
    WHEN `at the end of a section` THEN
        IF   theExpressionIndicatesThePenaltyAppliesOnlyToAProvisionOfTheSectionOrSubsection
        THEN `only the relevant provision of the section or subsection`
        ELSE `the whole section`
    WHEN `at the end of a subsection but not at the end of a section` THEN
        IF   theExpressionIndicatesThePenaltyAppliesOnlyToAProvisionOfTheSectionOrSubsection
        THEN `only the relevant provision of the section or subsection`
        ELSE `the whole subsection`
    WHEN `in a provision, other than at the end of a section or subsection` THEN `the provision in which the penalty is stated, or a stated part of it`

-- The two things a stated penalty can indicate, depending on whether the offence is expressly mentioned.
-- s 135 (3) speaks of "the provision (or a stated part of the provision)", s 134 (2) of "the section, subsection or relevant provision"; both reach subsection (4) of their section, which is the same rule.
DECLARE `What a stated penalty indicates` IS ONE OF
    `the offence is punishable on conviction as subsection (4) provides`
    `contravention is an offence punishable on conviction as subsection (4) provides`

-- src:1713 | (2) If an offence is not expressly mentioned in the section, subsection or relevant provision, the penalty indicates that contravention of the section, subsection or relevant provision is an offence punishable on conviction as provided by subsection (4).
@ref s 134 (2) (src:1713-1713)
-- src:1722 | (3) If an offence is expressly mentioned in the section, subsection or relevant provision, the penalty indicates that the offence is punishable on conviction as provided by subsection (4).
@ref s 134 (3) (src:1722-1722)
-- src:1752 | (2) If an offence is expressly mentioned in the provision, the penalty indicates that the offence is punishable on conviction as provided by subsection (4).
@ref s 135 (2) (src:1752-1752)
-- src:1755 | (3) If an offence is not expressly mentioned in the provision, the penalty indicates that contravention of the provision (or a stated part of the provision) is an offence punishable on conviction as provided by subsection (4).
@ref s 135 (3) (src:1755-1755)
GIVEN theOffenceIsExpresslyMentionedInTheSectionSubsectionOrProvision IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What a stated penalty indicates`
`s 134 (2), (3), s 135 (2), (3): what the stated penalty indicates` MEANS
    IF   theOffenceIsExpresslyMentionedInTheSectionSubsectionOrProvision
    THEN `the offence is punishable on conviction as subsection (4) provides`
    ELSE `contravention is an offence punishable on conviction as subsection (4) provides`

-- The penalty is a number in whatever unit it is stated (penalty units, months of imprisonment); a penalty of two kinds is checked one kind at a time.
-- src:1731 | (4) The penalty that may be imposed for the offence is—
-- src:1732 | (a) if only a single penalty is stated (whether as a maximum penalty or a penalty)—not more than the stated penalty; or
-- src:1733 | (b) if a minimum as well as a maximum penalty is stated—not less than the minimum and not more than the maximum.
@ref s 134 (4) (src:1731-1733)
-- src:1758 | (4) The penalty that may be imposed for the offence is—
-- src:1759 | (a) if only a single penalty is stated (whether as a maximum penalty or a penalty)—not more than the stated penalty; or
-- src:1760 | (b) if a minimum as well as a maximum penalty is stated—not less than the minimum and not more than the maximum.
@ref s 135 (4) (src:1758-1760)
GIVEN `maximum penalty stated` IS A NUMBER, `minimum penalty stated, if there is one` IS A MAYBE NUMBER, penalty IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 134 (4), s 135 (4): the penalty may be imposed` MEANS
    IF   penalty GREATER THAN `maximum penalty stated`
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER `minimum penalty stated, if there is one`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
         WHEN JUST least THEN penalty AT LEAST least

-- src:1734 | (5) If—
-- src:1735 | (a) a penalty (however expressed) is stated in a law at the end of a section divided into subsections; and
-- src:1736 | (b) another penalty (however expressed) is stated at the end of another subsection of the section; and
-- src:1737 | (c) the first penalty is not expressed in a way that indicates that it applies only to a particular provision of the last subsection;
-- src:1738 | the first penalty is taken, for this section, to be expressed in a way that indicates that it applies only to the last subsection.
@ref s 134 (5) (src:1734-1738)
GIVEN theFirstPenaltyIsStatedAtTheEndOfASectionDividedIntoSubsections IS A BOOLEAN, anotherPenaltyIsStatedAtTheEndOfAnotherSubsectionOfTheSection IS A BOOLEAN, theFirstPenaltyIsNotExpressedAsApplyingOnlyToAParticularProvisionOfTheLastSubsection IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 134 (5): the first penalty is taken to be expressed as applying only to the last subsection` MEANS
    IF   theFirstPenaltyIsStatedAtTheEndOfASectionDividedIntoSubsections AND anotherPenaltyIsStatedAtTheEndOfAnotherSubsectionOfTheSection AND theFirstPenaltyIsNotExpressedAsApplyingOnlyToAParticularProvisionOfTheLastSubsection
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Kind of material after a penalty` IS ONE OF
    `an example`
    `a note`
    `other text of the provision`

-- The material after the penalty is listed in order; the penalty is at the end if what follows it is only examples and notes.
-- src:1746 | (6) In working out for this section whether a penalty is at the end of a section or subsection, the position of any example or note is to be disregarded.
@ref s 134 (6) (src:1746-1746)
-- src:1761 | (5) In working out for this section whether a penalty is at the end of a section or subsection, the position of any example or note is to be disregarded.
@ref s 135 (5) (src:1761-1761)
GIVEN materialAfterThePenalty IS A LIST OF `Kind of material after a penalty`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 134 (6), s 135 (5): the penalty is at the end of the section or subsection` MEANS
    CONSIDER materialAfterThePenalty
    WHEN EMPTY THEN TRUE
    WHEN first FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        CONSIDER first
        WHEN `an example` THEN `s 134 (6), s 135 (5): the penalty is at the end of the section or subsection` rest
        WHEN `a note` THEN `s 134 (6), s 135 (5): the penalty is at the end of the section or subsection` rest
        WHEN `other text of the provision` THEN FALSE
